index 781a1a0..ef36d52 100644
--- a/docs/CLI.md
+++ b/docs/CLI.md
@@ -434,3 +434,33 @@ Targets that build on the device refuse while its PLC is RUNNING, exactly as the
 editor warns — on-device compilation can stall the build or make the running
 program miss scan deadlines. `--yes` / `-y` approves stopping it first, the way
 `apt install -y` does. Nothing stops a running PLC without being asked.
+
+## PLCdev candidate inspection (development bridge)
+
+`openplc-cli agent-candidate --json` is a read-only parent/child protocol for
+an isolated candidate created by the PLCdev task service. It neither connects
+to a running editor nor invokes a model, compiler, Runtime, device, or hardware.
+It does not offer apply, discard, or any write operation.
+
+The trusted parent starts a fresh process with `PLCDEV_AGENT_CANDIDATE_ROOT`
+set to the managed candidate root and `PLCDEV_AGENT_CAPABILITY` set to a newly
+generated 32-byte random token encoded as 64 lowercase hexadecimal characters.
+It writes one UTF-8 JSON request to stdin and closes stdin; the request is at
+most 16 KiB. Fields are `contractVersion` (1), `capability`, `taskId`,
+`projectId`, `candidateId`, `baselineRevision`, and `candidateDigest`. The
+parent must keep the token out of arguments, logs, project files, and receipts.
+A fresh process handles exactly one request; the caller must not reuse tokens.
+This is a parent-controlled local process boundary, not an OS isolation or
+protection against a hostile process running as the same user.
+
+The command checks the capability, confines and resolves the task/candidate
+path, rejects links, checks receipt identity and the baseline, and hashes every
+candidate project file before and after reading the native manifest and PLC
+project. A mismatch fails closed. The result labels the other editor's dirty
+state `unknown`; a separately hydrated headless copy cannot establish whether
+any GUI editor has unsaved buffers. Native manifest checks and digests are not
+compile, GUI edit, model generation, or runtime validation. An unavailable
+or unverifiable live editor state must never be treated as clean for an apply.
+
+The command is currently a source/development build capability; it has not yet
+been connected to the task service or shipped in the existing trial package.
